SUMMARY:Halloween
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY
DESCRIPTION:Halloween falls on October 31 and is\, by most measures\, the m
 ost widely observed non-federal holiday in the United States. It is also o
 ne of the least historically tidy: what Americans do on October 31 is a co
 mposite of a Gaelic harvest festival\, a Catholic feast\, Scottish and Iri
 sh neighborhood customs\, and a twentieth-century American candy industry 
 that found the whole thing extremely useful.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.co
 m/holiday/halloween/
