BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mardi-gras-20270209@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270209
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270210
SUMMARY:Mardi Gras
DESCRIPTION:Mardi Gras is Shrove Tuesday\, the day immediately before Ash W
 ednesday\, and the last day of the Carnival season. In Louisiana it is not
  a figure of speech but a statutory one: state law lists "the day of Mardi
  Gras" among the state's days of public rest and legal holidays. Almost ev
 erything Americans picture when they hear the word — krewes\, floats\, p
 urple and green and gold — was worked out in New Orleans between the 185
 0s and the 1880s.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/mardi-gras/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/mardi-gras/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
