DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20280117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280118
SUMMARY:Martin Luther King\, Jr. Day
DESCRIPTION:The federal holiday on the third Monday in January is\, in the 
 statute\, the Birthday of Martin Luther King\, Jr. — though almost every
 one says Martin Luther King\, Jr. Day. It took fifteen years to create: a 
 bill was introduced four days after King was killed in 1968 and died witho
 ut a vote\, and the law establishing the holiday was not signed until Nove
 mber 2\, 1983. Since 1994 federal law has also pointed the day toward comm
 unity service\, which makes it one of the few American holidays with an in
 struction attached.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/martin-luther-k
 ing-jr-day/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/martin-luther-king-jr-day
 /
CATEGORIES:Community
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
